Z||000005||87PegasusGT||04-11-2000||03:38 PM||||Yup. Thats exactly why I bought it. I just received it yesterday so shipping time to Oregon was exactly 1 week. website is:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.staffords-auto-parts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.staffords-auto-parts.com/</A> <BR>I spoke to Gino so if you tell them Dominic referred you, he will probably know what you want  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> He even offered to throw in the flywheel from a 93 Lumina at no cost, but did not have 1 in stock.<P>Anyway, hopefully engine will be installed by this time next week  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||04-11-2000||04:29 PM||||if you don't mind, i would like to ask a few quewtions?<P>1) the 3.4 liter fits in the 2.8 engine bay without any modifactions?  is this engine the same size (diminsionally) as the 2.8?<BR>2) what about the computer/wireing harness ect?  do these need to be carried over from the donor, or will the 2.8's work for this?<BR>3) how much horse power and torque do these engines produce?  can the getrag handle the torque?<BR>4)what do you need to do to drill starter holes?<BR>5)and is that <B>all</B> that needs to be done to fit this sucker into a fiero?<P>I am curious, as I will need to replace or rebuild my engine within the next 18 months.<P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000007||87PegasusGT||04-11-2000||06:47 PM||||These questions have been answered in previous posts, but here it is in a nutshell.<BR>EVERYTHING bolts together with no problems with these exceptions (even uses 2.8 Fiero plenum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">):<BR>Starter holes need to be drilled in 2.8 spot-<BR>Brackets need to be slightly modified-<BR>Injectors from 3.4 should be used/not 2.8<BR>Flywheel needs to be from an 88 Fiero GT/92-3 Lumina<BR>Starter area must be rounded off slightly to fit.<P>Everything here is simple enough that the normal mechanic can install the 3.4 WITHOUT a kit.<P>2.8 Computer/chip are used though I am getting a HO 2.8 chip and low temperature thermostat.<P>HP figures in Camaro are 160hp/ 195lbs torque.This translates into roughly 185hp in a Fiero with 0-60 in about 6.2 seconds with a stick. 200hp is easily attainable with this motor and NOS or Turbo allow from 150hp-300hp depending on boost,cooling, etc.<P>In other words, you can kiss an Integra Type R goodbye with no other mods  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||04-11-2000||10:33 PM||||hmmmm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>thanks!  as my car (when i ever get it running) will need a rebuild in the near future, i will keep this in mind!||||reg||1
Z||000009||87PegasusGT||04-12-2000||01:16 PM||||Whoops. I meant 250-300hp w NOS/Turbo||||reg||1
