Z||000011||JimIndyRCR||04-13-2000||01:16 PM||||I am new to the forum (so I missed all the previous how to's regarding the swap), looking to put a 3.4 into an 85 GT w/86 5speed- which flywheel should I use with this trans, and do I need a different p-plate and disc, how about wiring harness- use the 2.8 harness? Thanks for your help,<BR>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000012||lowCG||04-13-2000||01:33 PM||||From what I'm learning to use on my 3.4,which is a different 3.4 than yours,but is also an internally balanced engine,requiring an '88 Fiero flywheel,an early flywheel rebalanced to a nuetral balance,or some other nuetrally balanced unit from another V6.The  stock clutch pressure plate should be just fine,won't require any more pressure/stress on the hydraulics.However a disc with a performance lining(carbon fiber)and stronger springs is a good idea I've heard from Chris West who does these swaps for a living,he sells clutches,urethane motor mounts,other goodies to help with swaps too. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||87PegasusGT||04-13-2000||03:25 PM||||You can use a flexplate from an 88GT or any DOHC 3.4. No adaptors are needed though there is a slight area to be rounded off by the starter.||||reg||1
